<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomPermission xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        DISPOSITION GAP CLOSURE TRANCHE 1, ITEM 9 (agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t1-design.md
        §3 Item 9, decision D-7, settled at Gate 1 2026-08-31).

        WHY THIS EXISTS. Disposition__c.Record_Type_Is_Immutable (this same deploy) locks
        RecordTypeId once a disposition has committed past its opening stages - a validation rule
        is NOT bypassed by Modify All Data, so "admin-overridable" is unimplementable without a
        $Permission gate. This is that gate, built to the EXACT shape
        Account.Record_Type_Is_Immutable's own header prescribes: "If an exemption is ever
        needed, add a custom permission and gate on $Permission - never widen the rule itself."
        Account's own exemption custom permission,
        customPermissions/Lead_Convert_Account_RecordType_Stamp, is the structural template for
        this file.

        🔴 LOCK BOUNDARY - USER DECISION AT GATE 1, 2026-08-31, OVERRIDING THE DESIGN DOC'S OWN
        D-7 RECOMMENDATION (which proposed a looser boundary - see the validation rule's own XML
        comment for the full contrast). The disposition record type is changeable ONLY while
        Disposition_Stage__c is 'Disposition Readiness'; it is LOCKED from 'BOV Outreach' onward
        through 'Sale Closes'. Rationale, in the user's own terms: a principal approves a specific
        disposition path at Approval #1 (Sale_Decision_Approval, entry criterion
        Disposition_Stage__c = 'Disposition Readiness'), so nothing downstream of THAT approval
        may silently change it - "past Readiness" and "past the sale decision" are the same
        boundary. This custom permission is the ONLY admin escape from that lock - there is no
        other bypass.

        GRANT SCOPE - assigned in the consolidated permission-set pass (a separate file, owned by
        salesforce-solution-architect for this tranche), NOT here. Per the design doc: granted
        ONLY to DPEG_Admin_Access. ⚠ Per Lead_Convert_Account_RecordType_Stamp's own header,
        Modify All Data does NOT confer a custom-permission grant automatically - an admin who
        needs this override must actually hold the permission set carrying it, not merely
        System Administrator or Modify All Data.

        ⚠ $Permission gates by WHO the running user is, not by WHICH CODE PATH is running. Any
        holder of the granting permission set could in principle change an existing disposition's
        RecordTypeId by hand (UI edit, Data Loader) while this permission is active - the same
        accepted tradeoff Lead_Convert_Account_RecordType_Stamp's header records for its own
        equivalent gate. Do not grant this permission via any set other than the one the
        consolidated access pass names, without re-reading this note.

        🔴 THIS FILE MUST LAND IN THE SAME OR AN EARLIER DEPLOY THAN
        Disposition__c/validationRules/Record_Type_Is_Immutable.validationRule-meta.xml. A
        validation rule referencing {!$Permission.Disposition_Record_Type_Override} before the
        custom permission exists resolves the merge field to false for everyone, which is
        harmless (the rule just behaves as if nobody can ever override) - but if the ORDER is
        reversed in error and someone assumes the override is live before this permission is
        both deployed AND assigned, they will find the "admin escape" does not exist yet.
    -->
    <label>Disposition Record Type Override</label>
    <description>Exempts Disposition__c.Record_Type_Is_Immutable so an admin can change RecordTypeId after the disposition has locked (BOV Outreach onward, past the sale-decision approval). Granted only to DPEG_Admin_Access via the consolidated permission-set pass.</description>
    <isLicensed>false</isLicensed>
</CustomPermission>
